WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.048
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.348 --> 00:00:08.456
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.756 --> 00:00:14.845
Unit thirty: Global Citizenship. In this unit, you will discuss global issues and contrast ideas.

4
00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:16.990
global citizen.

5
00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:21.350
global citizen means a person who feels responsible for the whole world.

6
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:25.020
As global citizens, we should care about distant problems.

7
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.523
Your turn. Say: global citizen.

8
00:00:31.223 --> 00:00:32.456
global citizen.

9
00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.765
multiculturalism.

10
00:00:35.465 --> 00:00:39.368
multiculturalism means many cultures living together in one society.

11
00:00:39.668 --> 00:00:42.550
Singapore is famous for its multiculturalism.

12
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:46.169
Your turn. Say: multiculturalism.

13
00:00:48.869 --> 00:00:50.381
multiculturalism.

14
00:00:51.383 --> 00:00:52.559
globalisation.

15
00:00:53.259 --> 00:00:56.779
globalisation means the process of countries becoming more connected.

16
00:00:57.079 --> 00:00:59.961
Globalisation has brought foreign brands to every city.

17
00:01:00.661 --> 00:01:03.035
Your turn. Say: globalisation.

18
00:01:05.735 --> 00:01:07.026
globalisation.

19
00:01:08.017 --> 00:01:09.041
human dignity.

20
00:01:09.741 --> 00:01:13.587
human dignity means the value and respect every person deserves.

21
00:01:13.887 --> 00:01:17.314
Every refugee deserves to be treated with human dignity.

22
00:01:18.014 --> 00:01:20.736
Your turn. Say: human dignity.

23
00:01:23.436 --> 00:01:24.785
human dignity.

24
00:01:25.783 --> 00:01:26.877
cross-cultural.

25
00:01:27.577 --> 00:01:30.482
cross-cultural means involving two or more cultures.

26
00:01:30.782 --> 00:01:33.583
Working abroad improved her cross-cultural skills.

27
00:01:34.283 --> 00:01:36.552
Your turn. Say: cross-cultural.

28
00:01:39.252 --> 00:01:40.532
cross-cultural.

29
00:01:41.517 --> 00:01:42.715
world peace.

30
00:01:43.415 --> 00:01:45.775
world peace means a world without war.

31
00:01:46.075 --> 00:01:48.852
Many organisations work towards world peace.

32
00:01:49.552 --> 00:01:52.123
Your turn. Say: world peace.

33
00:01:54.823 --> 00:01:55.952
world peace.

34
00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.357
sustainable goals.

35
00:01:59.057 --> 00:02:03.669
sustainable goals means targets for a fairer, greener world by 2030.

36
00:02:03.969 --> 00:02:06.793
The UN's sustainable goals include ending poverty.

37
00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:10.296
Your turn. Say: sustainable goals.

38
00:02:12.996 --> 00:02:14.520
sustainable goals.

39
00:02:15.517 --> 00:02:17.296
international cooperation.

40
00:02:17.996 --> 00:02:21.261
international cooperation means countries working together.

41
00:02:21.561 --> 00:02:24.280
Climate change needs international cooperation.

42
00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:27.946
Your turn. Say: international cooperation.

43
00:02:30.646 --> 00:02:32.506
international cooperation.

44
00:02:33.517 --> 00:02:35.586
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:35.886 --> 00:02:41.345
Globalisation has many benefits, whereas some people say it destroys local culture.

46
00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:46.939
That's true. Despite the risks, it has reduced poverty in many countries.

47
00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:51.260
Nevertheless, inequality is still a huge problem.

48
00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:57.211
Agreed. That's why international cooperation and the sustainable goals matter.

49
00:02:58.517 --> 00:03:03.117
Being a global citizen means caring about human dignity everywhere.

50
00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:07.740
Exactly, and cross-cultural understanding is where it starts.

51
00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:13.255
Grammar focus: Linking contrast: whereas · despite · nevertheless.

52
00:03:13.555 --> 00:03:20.129
Use whereas to compare two facts, despite with a noun or -ing form, and nevertheless at the start of a new sentence.

53
00:03:20.429 --> 00:03:23.474
For example: Despite the rain, the festival continued.

54
00:03:23.774 --> 00:03:27.390
The plan is expensive. Nevertheless, it is necessary.

55
00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:33.683
Despite is followed by a noun or -ing, never by a full clause: despite raining ✓, despite it rained ✗.

56
00:03:34.683 --> 00:03:38.125
Now read and listen. Thinking Globally, Acting Locally.

57
00:03:38.425 --> 00:03:42.665
Globalisation connects people, products and ideas across the world.

58
00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:48.539
Despite these connections, many people still feel far from global problems.

59
00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:55.867
Global citizens believe that human dignity matters everywhere, whereas others focus only on their own country.

60
00:03:57.150 --> 00:04:02.934
The UN's sustainable goals encourage international cooperation on poverty, health and climate.

61
00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:07.991
Nevertheless, real change often starts with small local actions.

62
00:04:09.283 --> 00:04:11.762
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:04:12.062 --> 00:04:14.189
Countries becoming more connected is blank.

64
00:04:14.489 --> 00:04:18.885
A, globalisation. B, world peace. C, human dignity.

65
00:04:22.883 --> 00:04:25.463
The answer is A: globalisation.

66
00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:29.472
blank the heavy traffic, we arrived on time.

67
00:04:29.772 --> 00:04:33.600
A, Whereas. B, Despite. C, Nevertheless.

68
00:04:37.583 --> 00:04:39.316
The answer is B: Despite.

69
00:04:40.817 --> 00:04:43.675
My brother loves sport, blank I prefer reading.

70
00:04:43.975 --> 00:04:47.675
A, despite. B, whereas. C, nevertheless.

71
00:04:51.683 --> 00:04:53.671
The answer is B: whereas.

72
00:04:55.183 --> 00:04:57.554
Involving two or more cultures is blank.

73
00:04:57.854 --> 00:05:01.903
A, cross-cultural. B, sustainable. C, multiculturalism.

74
00:05:05.917 --> 00:05:08.357
The answer is A: cross-cultural.

75
00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:13.637
According to the text, real change often starts with blank.

76
00:05:13.937 --> 00:05:18.613
A, big governments. B, small local actions. C, international banks.

77
00:05:22.617 --> 00:05:25.882
The answer is B: small local actions.

78
00:05:27.383 --> 00:05:31.173
Now it's your turn to speak. What does being a global citizen mean to you?

79
00:05:36.473 --> 00:05:44.025
It means caring about people everywhere. Despite living in Cambodia, I can support global causes through my choices.

80
00:05:44.325 --> 00:05:45.802
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:46.817 --> 00:05:53.091
Great work today! You learned eight new words and linking contrast: whereas · despite · nevertheless.

82
00:05:53.391 --> 00:05:56.636
Today's value is kindness. Be kind to everyone.

83
00:05:56.936 --> 00:05:59.309
See you in Unit thirty-one. Goodbye!

84
00:05:59.609 --> 00:06:02.076
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

